# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines code ownership for automated review assignment.
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Patterns are evaluated top-to-bottom (last matching pattern takes precedence).
#
# A team that wants to own a folder adds a line here, for example `/osac-operator/ @osac-project/wg-vmaas`, in a pull
# request that wg-infra approves (see the self-protection rule below). From then on a change to that folder needs the
# approval of a member of that team, other than the author. The team must be visible and have write access to the
# repository (the wg-* teams do). Leave a folder out and any maintainer's approval is enough.

# CODEOWNERS Self-Protection
# Protects this file from unauthorized modification
/CODEOWNERS @osac-project/wg-infra
/osac-ui/ @LiorSoffer @batzionb @rawagner @ElayAharoni

# CI pipeline definition
# A pull request can change the workflows and scripts that produce the checks it is judged by, and then a passing
# check proves little. A change to them needs review from the infrastructure team. e2e-policy.yml decides which E2E suites a
# change needs.
/.github/workflows/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/actions/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/scripts/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/filters/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/e2e-policy.yml @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/ci-tests.yml @osac-project/wg-infra
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @osac-project/wg-infra
# The osac-ui lint and typecheck workflows run on pull_request, use no secret and report no required check, so the osac-ui
# maintainers (approvers in osac-ui/OWNERS) may approve them as well.
/.github/workflows/osac-ui-lint.yaml @osac-project/wg-infra @eliorerz @rawagner @ElayAharoni @batzionb @eranco74 @rccrdpccl
/.github/workflows/osac-ui-typecheck.yaml @osac-project/wg-infra @eliorerz @rawagner @ElayAharoni @batzionb @eranco74 @rccrdpccl
# Markdown inside those folders (a README) cannot change a check: a rule with no owner clears ownership.
/.github/**/*.md

# fullsend Configuration Protection
# Prevents pull_request_target misconfiguration and unauthorized workflow changes
# per ADR-0033 security requirements.
#
# These files control CI/CD execution with access to repository secrets.
# Changes require review from infrastructure team to prevent:
# - Credential exfiltration via pull_request_target
# - Unauthorized workflow modifications
# - Accidental security regressions
.github/workflows/fullsend.yaml @osac-project/wg-infra
.fullsend/ @osac-project/wg-infra
